       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Acetaminophen 10,000 mg three times daily comes to 30 g/day. That is about 7 times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day, and a single 10 g dose is already in the range that can cause severe hepatotoxicity. A 70 kg patient with normal liver function would still be at serious risk.\n\nDid you mean **1,000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3 g/day)? That's a common regimen. Other standard options are 650 mg every 6 hours or 500 mg every 6 hours.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 10,000 mg, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical reason. I would still advise against it."
