     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g/day. A single 10 g dose can cause acute liver failure, and no indication supports that dose. Entering it would very likely seriously harm or kill the patient.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours\n\nIf you meant a different amount, tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it. If the patient may have already taken a large amount of acetaminophen, that is an overdose. It needs urgent evaluation, including an acetaminophen level and consideration of N-acetylcysteine, and I'd recommend contacting poison control or toxicology. A medication order wouldn't address it.\n\nIf you want to pursue the original order anyway, please speak with your pharmacy team or attending first."
      }
     ],
